     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it may be an error.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. That's twice the labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin (2550 mg/day) and well above the maximum for extended-release (2000 mg/day). At that dose, the risk of GI side effects and lactic acidosis goes up a lot, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**What you might have meant:**\n- **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum). Writing \"1700\" for \"850\" is a common slip.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, split as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **1000 mg twice daily** (2000 mg/day), a common maintenance dose.\n\nCan you confirm the dose and formulation (IR or ER)? I'll enter it as soon as you do. If you really do mean 1700 mg three times daily, let me know the clinical reason and I can add a note to the order, though it will likely get flagged in pharmacy review."
      }
     ],
