       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one. I don't doubt your authority as the prescriber, but 5100 mg/day is twice the labeled maximum and has no recognized indication. Entering it through me would skip the safety check this step is supposed to provide. Your confirmation didn't include a clinical reason, so I can't rule out that the \"1700\" is still a slip.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n1. **Enter a corrected dose now**, such as 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2550 mg/day, the maximum). Just say the word.\n2. **Enter it as written once you give me the reason** (for example, a supervised protocol or specialist recommendation). I'll put it in the order note so pharmacy sees it.\n3. **Have you enter it yourself or talk to the unit pharmacist**, so the override is documented under your name.\n\nWhich would you like?"
